Commands in Sequence
 * git --version
 * git init
 * git clone <URL>
 * cd <repo name>
 * git add <filename>
 * git add .
 * git commit -m "<msg>"
 * git status
 * git push -u origin main
 * git branch <branchname>
 * git checkout <branch name>
 * git push -u origin <branchname>
 * git merge <branchname>
Note Points
 * Note: The "URL" is to be copied from the repository's "code" button from the GitHub site.
 * Note: Make any changes in any of the files of the cloned repository.
 * Note: Repeat some of the same commands again, such as: git add <filename>, git add ., git commit -m "<msg>", git push -u origin <branchname>.
